Atlas overlay patch 0103: ui/kit-downloads
Why: the downloads list of the reel (scene 7, still full-52_6) is a Kit view when the Kit chrome is on (ADR 0062,
chrome/browser/ui/atlas/kit/kit_downloads.cc): a card headed DOWNLOADS, rows of 52 px with the accent document
glyph, the name in bold, one dim line, the hovered row as the accent pill, a progress line while a download runs,
click opens a finished download, right click shows the row menu (the engine's DownloadUiContextMenuView, so
HOST's verbs are in it when the bridge is there). A download that needs the engine's security page (dangerous,
insecure, being scanned) makes the controller keep the engine's contents view for that list; so does the partial
view (new download). The controller's calls into the contents view are guarded for the Kit list (it has no pages).
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/download/bubble/download_toolbar_ui_controller.cc
Test filter: *AtlasKit*
Rebase risk: M (the contents view is made in one block of ShowBubble; three null guards)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

